-- media_environment
INSERT INTO media_environment (id, country_id, legal_environment, media_regulators, journalists_associations, radio_stations, tv_stations, newspapers, state_owned_media, news_agency, international_media, online_media, internet_freedom, leading_media, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(3, 3, '<p>Free expression, including media freedom, in Benin is primarily guaranteed by the 1990 <a href="https://www.refworld.org/legal/legislation/natlegbod/1990/fr/14505">Constitution</a> (revised 2019) through Article 24. It is also protected by specific laws including the <a href="https://sgg.gouv.bj/doc/loi-2015-07/">Information and Communication Code of 2015</a> and the <a href="https://sgg.gouv.bj/doc/loi-organique-92-021/">Organic Law N&deg;92-021 of August 21, 1992</a> which established <a name="_Hlk202438676"></a>the <a href="https://haac.bj/">High Authority of Audiovisuals and Communications (HAAC).</a><!-- [if !supportNestedAnchors]--><a name="_Hlk202438200"></a><!--[endif]--></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Additionally, digital code&nbsp;<a href="https://cyrilla.org/entity/gwed8gwpzgv?page=111&amp;file=1599162145907mfuegng01im.pdf">Law No. 2017-20</a> of April 20, 2018, addresses digital rights and freedoms, including provisions related to data protection. While it doesn''t strictly require a Data Protection Officer (DPO) for all organizations, appointing one can exempt organizations from certain notification requirements.&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Benin however has a <a href="https://droit-et-politique-en-afrique.info/code-penal-de-la-republique-du-benin-du-28-decembre-2018">penal code</a> that includes provisions against divulging &ldquo;professional secrets&rdquo; by civil servants. Defamation, governed by Law 2015-07, is no longer punishable by imprisonment, however, it can impose very heavy fines.</p>', '<p> he main media regulatory body in Benin is the <a href="https://haac.bj/">High Authority of Audiovisuals and Communications (HAAC).</a>, which oversees the country''s audiovisual and communication sectors, including press and online media.&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Another important regulator is the&nbsp;<a href="https://service.apdp.bj/">Authority for the Protection of Personal Data (APDP),</a> an independent administrative body ensuring compliance with the Digital Code and the right to privacy, while the <a href="https://arcep.bj/">Regulatory Authority for Electronic Communications and Post Office (ARCEP)</a> is responsible for the regulation of electronic communications and postal services.&nbsp;</p>', '<p><a href="https://web.facebook.com/p/Union-des-Professionnels-des-M%C3%A9dias-du-B%C3%A9nin-UPMB-100057510078477/?locale=fr_FR&amp;_rdc=1&amp;_rdr">Union des Professionnels des M&eacute;dias du B&eacute;nin (UPMB),</a> works to advance the interests of media professionals in Benin.&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Observatoire de la D&eacute;ontologie et de l''Ethique dans les M&eacute;dias (ODEM) is a self-regulatory body focused on promoting professionalism and ensuring adherence to ethical codes within the Beninese media landscape.&nbsp;ODEM also aims to identify media abuses and enhance professional skills through training.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><a href="https://web.facebook.com/acjuniben/?_rdc=1&amp;_rdr">Association of Campus Journalist University of Benin</a> (UniBen) is an association of student journalists at the University of Benin.</p>', '<p>Benin has&nbsp;at least 70&nbsp;private and community radio stations.</p>', '<p>Benin has about 22  V stations, including the National broadcaster Benin TV.</p>', '<p> he country has about 100 newspapers, including the government daily,&nbsp;<a href="https://lanation.bj/">La Nation</a>, as well as privately owned ones, including&nbsp;Le Matin, Le Matinal, Fraternit&eacute;&nbsp;and&nbsp;La Nouvelle Tribune.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Benin also has the national newswire service, <a href="https://x.com/abpbj?lang=en">Agence B&eacute;nin Presse (ABP</a>).</p>', '<p>Benin&rsquo;s primary television broadcaster is the state-owned <a href="https://srtb.bj/accueil/">Soci&eacute;t&eacute; de radio et de t&eacute;l&eacute;vision du B&eacute;nin (SR B)</a> formerly ORTB, which operates the main channel, Benin TV and Benin TV Junior. The ORTB operates its own 5 radio stations that broadcast in 18 languages. There are also 104 FM transmitters for various stations throughout the country.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Additionally, the state runs <a href="https://lanation.bj/">La Nation</a>, the national broadsheet.</p>', '<p><span lang="EN-US">In 2022, the government shut down the national news agency <a href="https://www.banouto.bj/article/politique/20220117-media-le-gouvernement-de-patrice-talon-dissout-lagence-benin-presse-abp">Agence Benin-Press (ABP)</a>.</span></p>', '<p><span lang="EN-US">While Benin is a separate country, several Nigerian  V stations also broadcast within the region, including BS-Benin, NTA-Benin, NTA-Iruekpen, AIT-Benin, and STV-Benin. There is also Canal 3, a French channel.</span></p>', '<p>Oline media in Benin is mainly made up of websites of traditional media outlets and social media platforms. <a href="https://www.einpresswire.com/world-media-directory/3/benin"> here are several of these</a>.</p>', '<p>Internet shutdowns are not frequent in Benin, with <a href="https://www.internetsociety.org/blog/2021/06/keeping-the-internet-on-during-benins-presidential-elections/">a 2019 partial shutdown during parliamentary elections</a>, being the most significant government meddle with the internet. However, through its Digital Code, which criminalizes false news, the state does <a href="https://mfwa.org/country-highlights/benins-digital-code-must-be-reviewed-to-protect-freedom-of-expression-online-mfwa/">prosecute journalists</a> who are deemed to have churned and disseminated false news.</p>', '<p><a href="https://lanouvelletribune.info/">&nbsp;La Nouvelle  ribune,</a> <a href="https://lanation.bj/">La Nation,</a> <a href="http://levenementprecis.com/">L''Evenement Precis,</a> <a href="https://matinlibre.com/">Matin Libre,&nbsp;</a><a href="http://www.fraternitebj.info/">Fraternite,&nbsp;</a><a href="https://ortb.bj/">Television Nationale,</a> Canal 3, Golfe TV, Carrefour TV Radio, <a href="https://ortb.bj/">Radio Nationale,</a> <a href="http://www.cappfm.com/">CAPP FM,&nbsp;</a><a href="https://radiotokpa.info/">Radio Tokpa,&nbsp;</a>Golfe FM, <a href="http://ric.immacolata.com/">Radio Immaculee Conception,</a> <a href="https://www.24haubenin.info/">24 Heures Au Benin,&nbsp;</a><a href="https://www.banouto.info/">Banouto,</a> <a href="https://beninwebtv.com/">Benin Web TV</a>.</p>', '2025-09-08 17:06:38.722429', '2025-11-18 13:14:11.173312'),
(4, 4, '<p> he primary guarantor of press freedom in Burkina Faso is the <a href="https://www.constituteproject.org/constitution/Burkina_Faso_2015">1991 Constitution (reviewed in 2015)</a>, specifically through Article 8, which guarantees freedom of opinion, expression, and the press, as well as the right to information.&nbsp; In addition, <a href="chrome-extension://efaidnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/https:/www.freedominfo.org/wp-content/uploads/Loi-051-portant-sur-lacc--s----linformation-publique.pdf">Loi 051 portant sur l''acc&egrave;s &agrave; l''information publique (Law 051 on Access to Public Information)</a> provides the specific mechanisms for exercising the right to access information.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Defamation is no longer a criminal offense, following decriminalization in 2014. However, under the country&rsquo;s Penal Code (<a href="chrome-extension://efaidnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/file:/C:/Users/23354/Downloads/CODE%20PENAL%20du%20Burkina%20Faso.pdf">Code Penal du Burkina Faso</a>), defamation can attract hefty fines.</p>', '<p> he <a href="https://www.csc.gov.bf/accueil">Conseil Sup&eacute;rieur de la Communication (CSC)</a> is the media regulator in Burkina Faso. In November 2023, <a href="https://mfwa.org/country-highlights/new-law-puts-burkina-fasos-media-regulator-under-junta-control/">a new law was passed by the military junta</a> which exaggerated the powers of the Head of State over the Council, allowing him to appoint the CSC&rsquo;s President.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>In addition to the CSC, the <a href="https://www.arcep.bf/">Autorit&eacute; de r&eacute;gulation des communications &eacute;lectroniques et des Postes (ARCEP)</a> regulates the broadcasting sector through licensure and compliance enforcement. ARCEP also monitors the frequency spectrum, resolves disputes, and encourages the development of new equipment.</p>', '<p>Media Associations in Burkina Faso include the <a href="https://base.afrique-gouvernance.net/fr/corpus_organismes/fiche-organismes-118.html">Association des Journalistes du Burkina (AJB),</a> this is the main association for journalists in Burkina Faso. However, in March 2025, <a href="https://mfwa.org/country-highlights/burkina-faso-journalists-association-dissolution-press-freedom/">the military junta dissolved the AJB</a></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Syndicat Autonome des  ravailleurs de l''Information et de la Culture (SYNATIC), is a trade union for media professionals representing the interests of workers in the information and culture sectors.&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Observatoire Burkinab&eacute; des M&eacute;dias (OBM) focuses on monitoring the media landscape in Burkina Faso, promoting media freedom and ethical reporting.&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Centre National de la Presse Norbert Zongo (CNP-NZ), this center works to promote media freedom, freedom of expression, and investigative journalism.&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Union Nationale de l''Audiovisuel Libre du Faso (UNALFA) represents independent audiovisual media outlets in Burkina Faso.&nbsp;</p>', '<p>It is estimated that there are some 185 radio stations in Burkina Faso.</p>', '<p> here are 13 television stations in Burkina Faso, including 8 public and 5 private stations,&nbsp;<a href="https://www.cinergie.bf/spip.php?article829">according to the High Council for Communication (CSC)</a>.&nbsp;</p>', '<p>It is estimated that there are more than 80 newspapers in the country.  his includes both state-owned and private titles.</p>', '<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><a href="https://www.rtb.bf/">Radiodiffusion  &eacute;l&eacute;vision du Burkina (RTB</a>) is the main state broadcaster, providing both radio and television services.&nbsp;RTB runs <a href="http://www.rtb.bf/">Radio Burkina,&nbsp;</a>as well as entertainment station <a href="https://radioarcenciel.re/">Canal Arc-en-Ciel</a>. RTB also runs the national television broadcaster, <a href="http://www.rtb.bf/">Television Nationale du Burkina</a>.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><a href="https://www.sidwaya.info/">Sidwaya</a> is the state-run national newspaper.</p>', '<p>Burkina Faso also has a national news agency, <a href="https://www.aib.media/">Agence d''Information du Burkina</a>.</p>', '<p><a href="https://www.bbc.com/audio/stations">BBC</a> is available on FM in Ouagadougou.&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><a href="https://www.voanews.com/">Voice of America (VOA)</a> operates a full-time relay in the country but has faced suspensions for broadcasting content deemed critical of the military junta.&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><a href="https://www.dw.com/en/top-stories/s-9097">Deutsche Welle (DW)</a> the German broadcaster broadcasts in Burkina Faso but has also been suspended by the Burkinab&eacute; government.&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><a href="https://www.lemonde.fr/en/burkina-faso/">Le Monde</a> a French newspaper, publishes in Burkina Faso but has also been targeted by the government''s suspensions, particularly for its reporting on the conflict and human rights issues.&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/burkina-faso"> he Guardian</a>, a British newspaper was also among those suspended for reporting on the Human Rights Watch report.&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<p> he online media landscape in Burkina Faso is a very active and diverse one, mainly made up of legacy media websites and news portals, and portals that belong to independent media organizations.</p>', '<p>Internet freedom is limited.  he Higher Council of Communication and the chief prosecutor monitor internet websites and discussion forums on state-sanctioned fishing expedition for anti-junta detractors. When it deems fit, the authorities <a href="https://www.africanews.com/2021/11/25/burkina-faso-extends-internet-suspension/">shut down the internet</a>. Also, the <a href="https://2021-2025.state.gov/reports/2023-country-reports-on-human-rights-practices/burkina-faso/#:~:text=within%20the%20army.-,Internet%20Freedom,to%20enforce%20compliance%20with%20regulations.">law permits a judge, to block internet websites or email addresses being used to spread &ldquo;false information&rdquo; to the public, at the request of a prosecutor.&nbsp;</a></p>', '<p>Radiodiffusion  &eacute;l&eacute;vision du Burkina (RTB), Agence d''Information du Burkina (AIB),&nbsp;Sidwaya, <a href="https://web.facebook.com/evenementbf/?locale=fr_FR&amp;_rdc=1&amp;_rdr">L''&Eacute;v&eacute;nement</a>, <a href="https://lepays.bf/">Le Pays</a>, <a href="https://www.omegamedias.info/">Omega FM,</a> <a href="https://www.monpulsar.com/">Radio Pulsar</a>, <a href="https://onlineradiobox.com/bf/horizon/?lang=en">Horizon FM</a>, <a href="https://web.facebook.com/ouagafm/videos/?_rdc=1&amp;_rdr">Ouaga FM</a>, Faso.net, <a href="https://faso7.com/">Faso 7</a>, <a href="https://burkina24.com/">Burkina 24</a>, and <a href="https://sahelien.com/en/">Sahelien</a>, <a href="https://cenozo.org/promotion-of-investigative-journalism-in-west-africa-what-results-in-2024/">CENOZO</a>, <a href="https://www.bamyinga.com/">Bam Yinga</a>.</p>', '2025-09-08 17:06:38.722429', '2025-12-09 14:49:14.9141'),
(5, 5, '<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US" style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;">Free expression, including press freedom is guaranteed<strong> </strong>by<strong> </strong>the<strong> </strong></span><a href="https://www.constituteproject.org/constitution/Cape_Verde_1992"><span lang="EN-US" style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;">1980 Constitution (rev. 1992</span><strong><span lang="EN-US" style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;">)</span></strong></a><strong><span lang="EN-US" style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;">, </span></strong><span lang="EN-US" style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-ansi-language: EN-US;">specifically by<strong> </strong></span><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">Article 27 which provides for the freedom of thought, association, religion, and other fundamental freedoms as well.  he Constitution also provides for freedom of the press and confidentiality of journalistic sources. Through the </span><a href="chrome-extension://efaidnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/https:/dataprotection.africa/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/Cabo-Verde_DPA.pdf"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">Data Protection Act</span></a><strong><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;"> <span style="mso-spacerun: yes;">&nbsp;</span></span></strong><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;"><span style="font-family: ''Calibri'',sans-serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; color: #001d35; background: white;">(Law 133/V/2001) access to information is guaranteed.</span></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; color: #001d35; background: white;">Defamation is a criminal offence<strong>.</strong> Articles 184, 185, and <strong>186</strong> of the<strong> </strong></span><a href="chrome-extension://efaidnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/https:/policehumanrightsresources.org/content/uploads/2016/07/Penal-Code-Cape-Verde-2003-Good-version.pdf?x80005"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; background: white;">Penal Code</span></a><strong><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; color: #001d35; background: white;"> </span></strong><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; color: #001d35; background: white;">criminalizes defamation<strong>. </strong></span><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">Even though a constitutional amendment in 1999 excluded freedom of expression as a defence in defamation cases, there have been no libel cases since 2002, indicating a potential shift in practice or interpretation.</span></p>', '<p><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: ''Calibri'',sans-serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;"> he primary media regulatory authority is the&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: ''Calibri'',sans-serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-font-family: ''Times New Roman''; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;"><a href="https://www.arme.cv/"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">Ag&ecirc;ncia Reguladora Multissectorial da Economia (ARME)</span><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">&nbsp;</span></a></span><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: ''Calibri'',sans-serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;">(Multisector Regulatory Agency of the Economy).&nbsp;ARME is responsible for regulating the communications sector, including media, as part of its broader role in regulating various economic sectors</span></p>', '<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;"> he<strong>&nbsp;</strong></span><a href="https://web.facebook.com/jornalistascaboverdeajoc/?locale=pt_BR&amp;_rdc=1&amp;_rdr"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">Associa&ccedil;&atilde;o Sindical dos Jornalistas de Cabo Verde (AJOC)</span><strong><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">,</span></strong></a><strong><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;"> </span></strong><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">(Cape Verde Journalists'' Union Association)</span><strong><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">&nbsp;</span></strong><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">&nbsp;is a non-profit organization representing journalists from press, radio, television, news agencies, and online media. It focuses on advocating for the social and professional integration of all Cape Verdean journalists. </span></p>', '<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;"> here are some 20 radio stations in Cape Verde, comprising private and state-owned broadcasters.</span></p>', '<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;"> here are </span><a href="https://www.tvchannellists.com/w/List_of_channels_on_digital_terrestrial_television_in_Cape_Verde"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">about 18</span></a><strong><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;"> </span></strong><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">Tv stations in Cape Verde.</span></p>', '<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;"> here some 9 newspapers in Cape Verde, with 3 main weekly publications: A Na&ccedil;&atilde;o, A Semana, and Expresso das Ilhas.</span></p>', '<p class="MsoNormal"><a href="http://www.rtc.cv/"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;"> CV</span><strong><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">,&nbsp;</span></strong></a><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">is the national television broadcaster, operated by Radiotelevisao Caboverdiana.</span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a href="http://www.rtc.cv/"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">RCV,</span><strong><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">&nbsp;</span></strong></a><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">is state-run national television broadcaster, operated by Radiotelevisao Caboverdiana.</span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a href="https://www.novojornal.co.ao/politica/detalhe/cabo-verde-pode-contar-com-tudo-o-que-for-possivel-de-angola---joao-lourenco-pede-accao-concertada-e-solucoes-locais-para-conflitos-em-africa-28977.html"><em><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">Novo Jornal-Cabo Verde</span></em></a><strong><em><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">, </span></em></strong><em><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">is </span></em>the state-run newspaper (published twice weekly).</p>', '<p class="MsoNormal"><a href="https://web.facebook.com/groups/2188291054819562"><span style="mso-comment-reference: SA_1; mso-comment-date: 20250815 1314;"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">Ag&ecirc;ncia Cabo-verdiana de Not&iacute;cias</span></span></a><!-- [if !supportNestedAnchors]--><!--[endif]--><span class="MsoCommentReference"><span style="font-size: 8.0pt; line-height: 115%;"><!-- [if !supportAnnotations]--><a id="_anchor_1" class="msocomanchor" href="#_msocom_1" name="_msoanchor_1">[SA1]</a><!--[endif]--><span style="mso-special-character: comment;">&nbsp;</span></span></span><strong><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">, </span></strong><span style="mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;">is the national news agency.<strong>&nbsp;</strong></span></p>
