</div>', '<p><a href="https://standard.gm/"> he Standard,&nbsp;</a><a href="https://foroyaa.net/">Foroyaa,&nbsp;</a><a href="https://thepoint.gm/">The Point,&nbsp;</a><a href="https://freedomnewspaper.gm/">Freedom Newspaper,</a> <a href="http://www.grts.gm/">Gambia Television (GRTS TV),&nbsp;</a><a href="http://www.grts.gm/">Radio Gambia,&nbsp;</a><a href="https://westcoast.gm/">West Coast Radio,</a> <a href="https://www.facebook.com/capitalfm100.4/">Capital FM,&nbsp;</a><a href="https://www.facebook.com/uniquefm.gambia/">Unique FM,&nbsp;</a><a href="http://www.paradisefm.gm/">Paradise FM,&nbsp;</a><a href="http://www.jollofnews.com/">Joll Of News,&nbsp;</a><a href="https://www.fatunetwork.net/">Fatu Network,&nbsp;</a></p>', '2025-09-08 17:06:38.722429', '2025-11-19 12:29:58.769514'),
(18, 18, '<p>Free expression, along with free press, are guaranteed by <a href="https://www.constituteproject.org/constitution/ ogo_2007">Article 26 of the 1992 (rev 2007) Constitution</a>. Specifically, the media in Togo is governed by a media code which emanates from Law No.98-004/PR. Journalists must also abide by a <a href="https://accountablejournalism.org/ethics-codes/Togo-Journalists">Press and Communications Code of Ethics.</a>&nbsp; While imprisonment for defamation was abolished in August 2004, journalists can still receive a criminal fine of up to 5 million CFA francs ($10,000) under Article 104 of the media code or Article 58 of the penal code.</p>', '<p> he <a href="https://www.haactogo.tg/">High Authority of Broadcasting and Communications (HAAC)&nbsp;</a>is the main media regulator in Togo<span lang="EN-US">. There is also</span> <span lang="EN-US">the </span>Togolese Media Observatory, which is an organ established by the media practitioners themselves to instill self-discipline within the profession.</p>', '<p><span lang="EN-US"> he main media association in Togo is the </span><a href="https://web.facebook.com/p/UJIT-TOGO-61551629025374/?_rdc=1&amp;_rdr">Union des journalistes Ind&eacute;pendants du Togo (UJIT)</a><span lang="EN-US">. There is also the </span>National Council of Press Magnates (CONAPP), Union of Public Media Information Agents, Technicians and Journalists (SAINT JOP), Togolese Observatory for the Image of Women in the Media (OTIFEM), Association of Cinematographic Critics of Togo (AJCC &mdash; TOGO), Network of Economic Journalists of Togo (RJE &mdash; TOGO), Free Communications Union (SYNLICO), Journalists for Human Rights (JDHO) and, finally, the Association of Environmental Journalists.</p>', '<p> ogo has some 94 radio stations.</p>', '<p> ogo has about 6 television stations.</p>', '<p> ogo has some 234 newspapers and magazines.</p>', '<p><a href="https://togopresse.tg/"><span lang="EN-US"> ogo Presse</span></a><span lang="EN-US"> is the national broadsheet owned and operated by the State. The State also </span><span lang="EN-US">&nbsp;owns and operates, </span><a href="https://www.youtube.com/c/TelevisonTogolaise">T&eacute;l&eacute;vision Togolaise<span lang="EN-US">, </span></a><span lang="EN-US">t</span><span lang="EN-US">he national television broadcaster and </span>Radio Togolaise - state-run national radio, via shortwave, mediumwave (AM) and FM<span lang="EN-US">, and </span><a href="https://radiolome.tg/"><span lang="EN-US">Radio Lome FM</span></a><span lang="EN-US">.</span></p>', '<p><a href="https://atop.tg/">Agence  ogolaise de Presse,&nbsp;external</a>&nbsp;- state news agency is the national newswire service.</p>', '<p><a href="https://www.rfi.fr/fr/tag/togo/"><span lang="FR">Radio France Internationale (RFI)</span></a></p>', '<p><span lang="EN-US">Online media is a key part of the media mix in  ogo with this variety of media mostly made up of websites and news portals of legacy media organizations. Key among the media outlets here is </span><a href="https://togoweb.net/"><span lang="EN-US">Togoweb</span></a><span lang="EN-US">.</span></p>', '<p> ogo&rsquo;s government restricted internet access, including disruptions to social media platforms like Facebook, Signal, and Telegram, in 2025. These restrictions were implemented after protests, says a report by the Media Foundation.</p>', '<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; background: white; vertical-align: baseline;"><span style="color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;"><a href="http://togopresse.tg/"><strong><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: '' imes New Roman''; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin; color: #3483d4; border: none windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-alt: none windowtext 0in; padding: 0in; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB;">Togo-Presse,</span></strong></a></span><span style="font-size: 12.0pt; mso-farea